{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778601720020,"sessionID":"ses_1e3157ae4ffeLbRDIq24x1i8aY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-92e4dc412a08d80e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__agent_prompt__.md"},"output":"<path>/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__agent_prompt__.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: Your job is to address issue #3267.\n2: First, read the file __issue_context__.json in the current working directory to get the issue title, body, and comments.\n3: \n4: IMPORTANT: You are working in a local copy of ai4curation/eval-ont-agent-cl.\n5: The issue context was imported from obophenotype/cell-ontology for evaluation purposes.\n6: Do NOT attempt to clone, checkout, or interact with any remote repositories.\n7: Stay in the current working directory and make all changes here.\n8: \n9: On completion, commit your changes locally. Do NOT push - that will be handled automatically.\n10: Don't commit files you did not edit.\n11: \n12: After committing, create two files:\n13: \n14: 1. ISSUE_COMMENTS.md: Updates on the issue regarding its status. This will be fed back to the originating issue.\n15: 2. PR_COMMENTS.md: A description of your changes, and the rationale. This will be fed back to the originating PR.\n16: \n17: I will take care of feeding these back to the GitHub repo, you just need to create them. Don't commit them,\n18: and don't attempt to interact with the github repo.\n19: \n20: If the original issue is not clear, ask for clarification in ISSUE_COMMENTS.md, and do not\n21: commit any changes. The PR_COMMENTS.md can be empty in this case.\n22: \n23: Your PR_COMMENTS.md should be a human-readable description of your changes, and the rationale. Include any checklists\n24: you created for yourself and completed. If you performed validation, background research, etc, be sure to mention this.\n25: \n26: Your ISSUE_COMMENTS.md need not replicate what is in PR_COMMENTS.md, and in many cases can be terse but polite, e.g\n27: \"changes committed in PR #<NN>\" (note: use the literal `<NN>` in the output, I will replace it with the actual PR number).\n28: \n29: If the issue is a complex one, you can create a high level summary of the decisions you made. If things are not clear\n30: or if you want particular people in the thread to check particular aspects you can mention them.\n31: \n32: Follow any CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md or other relevant files in the repository.\n\n(End of file - total 32 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"Your job is to address issue #3267.\nFirst, read the file __issue_context__.json in the current working directory to get the issue title, body, and comments.\n\nIMPORTANT: You are working in a local copy of ai4curation/eval-ont-agent-cl.\nThe issue context was imported from obophenotype/cell-ontology for evaluation purposes.\nDo NOT attempt to clone, checkout, or interact with any remote repositories.\nStay in the current working directory and make all changes here.\n\nOn completion, commit your changes locally. Do NOT push - that will be handled automatically.\nDon't commit files you did not edit.\n\nAfter committing, create two files:\n\n1. ISSUE_COMMENTS.md: Updates on the issue regarding its status. This will be fed back to the originating issue.\n2. PR_COMMENTS.md: A description of your changes, and the rationale. This will be fed back to the originating PR.\n\nI will take care of feeding these back to the GitHub repo, you just need to create them. Don't commit them,\nand don't attempt to interact with the github repo.\n\nIf the original issue is not clear, ask for clarification in ISSUE_COMMENTS.md, and do not","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"__agent_prompt__.md","time":{"start":1778601720014,"end":1778601720019}},"id":"prt_e1cec76e6001j20k5t1H5QGG53","sessionID":"ses_1e3157ae4ffeLbRDIq24x1i8aY","messageID":"msg_e1cec4a1e001l1ulpGkvuOBOhI"}}
