{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778601766062,"sessionID":"ses_1e3157ae4ffeLbRDIq24x1i8aY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8970e907e2abc042","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/CLAUDE.md","pattern":"dragon-ai-agent"},"output":"Found 1 matches\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json:\n  Line 2:   \"body\": \"**Problems**\\n- In the current claude.md file, the agent is instructed to sign off as @dragon-ai-agent. \\n- The agent sometimes adds` AnnotationAssertion(dc:contributor obo:CL_0010000 \\\"dragon-ai-agent\\\") ` when updating the textual def of a term which:\\n1) fails the QC\\n2)In CL, we use `dcterms:contributor` only when creating a new term \\n\\n\\n**Changes**\\nUpdate claude.md - ie. \\n1) always sign your commits `GitHub Copilot`\\n2) Change ` created_by: dragon-ai-agent` to `dc:creator GitHub Copilot` and make it clear only to use this when creating new terms \\n\\n\\n**Another problem**\\n- Co-pilot only looks at CL ids in the cl-edit file when generating a new ID (so does not take into account Ids assigned in open PRs) - This has been fixed by Damien's implementation\\n\\n\\n\",\n","metadata":{"matches":1,"truncated":false},"title":"dragon-ai-agent","time":{"start":1778601766026,"end":1778601766060}},"id":"prt_e1ced2a1b001opaYhJVa5dXFf4","sessionID":"ses_1e3157ae4ffeLbRDIq24x1i8aY","messageID":"msg_e1cec793a001hxVbWOuix75da0"}}
